ode observations, not a completed safety argument. Caller-owned disk and transport are explicit in the README; the async interface specifically requires reliable in-order processing per local storage target, allows cross-target reordering, and requires durability before append responses. Early sourced surface: README.md:118 permits sending Messages while entries in the same Ready are being persisted, whereas node.go:74-75,100-101 requires persistence before sending. rawnode.go:177-185 relies on the stronger Ready contract when exposing msgsAfterAppend. Both statements are retained; no execution legality or violation is inferred from choosing one.\",\n        \"remaining\": [\n          \"Core gap: read campaign, election tally, leader append-response aggregation, follower append acceptance and log commit checks to establish the complete A1 formation path.\",\n          \"Core gap: read membership application, joint quorum, snapshot restore, Storage reconstruction and Node serialization to explain eligible support across authority and configuration transitions.\",\n          \"Core gap: trace read-index pending requests, leadership transfer, timers and committed-entry consumption, including callers and completion duties.\",\n          \"Contract surface: resolve the README/Ready same-batch persistence-order discrepancy before using overlap as a legal failure history; inspect examples, Node interface documentation and actual publication consumers.\",\n          \"Local unknown: reset retains pendingReadIndexMessages outside readOnly; its producer, release and context handling have not yet been read, so no claim about stale pending read requests is made.\"\n        ],\n        \"understanding\": \"updated\",\n        \"rationale\": \"Complete the backbone through aggregation and configuration before selecting a principal Fact. The persistence contract discrepancy is a concrete source lead to retain, but further contract and consumer reading is cheaper and more discriminating than an execution that assumes the disputed caller schedule.\",\n        \"question_updates\": {}\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"pending_work\": [],\n  \"current\": {\n    \"phase\": \"executed\",\n    \"operation_id\": \"aab7e39abde64d94a6f6bd461631f9d5\",\n    \"action\": \"research\"\n  },\n  \"latest_decision\": {\n    \"operation_id\": \"aab7e39abde64d94a6f6bd461631f9d5\",\n    \"action\": \"research\",\n    \"record\": {\n      \"path\": \"state.json\",\n      \"collection\": \"selections\",\n      \"match\": {\n        \"operation_id\": \"aab7e39abde64d94a6f6bd461631f9d5\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"stop\": {},\n  \"stop_reason\": \"Not started\",\n  \"explorations\": [],\n  \"review_issues\": [],\n  \"run_id\": \"66f2e4acc7af4e289b0684fcbcf1574d\",\n  \"snapshot_id\": \"e9acf66cb36d4c969c0544c6fedb2015\",\n  \"elapsed_seconds\": 150.64584290499624,\n  \"source_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_22-35-07-etcd_raft-real-run/agent-source\",\n  \"draft_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_22-35-07-etcd_raft-real-run/draft\",\n  \"state_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_22-35-07-etcd_raft-real-run/state.json\",\n  \"product_schemas\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_22-35-07-etcd_raft-real-run/product-schemas.json\",\n  \"submission_schema\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_22-35-07-etcd_raft-real-run/submission.schema.json\",\n  \"method_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_22-35-07-etcd_raft-real-run/audit-method.md\",\n  \"directed_question\": null,\n  \"tools\": {\n    \"agent\": \"codex-cli 0.155.0-alpha.16\",\n    \"implementation\": \"go version go1.26.7 linux/amd64\"\n  },\n  \"implementation\": {\n    \"name\": \"go_module\",\n    \"harness_kind\": \"go_test\",\n    \"harness_filename\": \"assurance_generated_test.go\",\n    \"instructions\": \"Use TestAssurance-prefixed Go tests i